{
  "_about": "B83: a request-box question or a Flint inbox answer (anything that isn't /build). Launched with --permission-mode dontAsk, so what isn't allowed here is refused without asking: these runs read the tree, write the planning files and the outbox, and run the read-only checks the inbox prompt names. The deny block below takes back the allow rules ~/projects/.claude/settings.json would otherwise hand them (site, client, newsletter, the relay, push, PR create and merge, systemctl, the whole playwright server) — an answer to a question needs none of them. `todo doctor` lists any project allow rule this file hasn't been reviewed against (headless/inherited.json).",
